        "theme":  "Platforms",
        "summary":  "Anthropic updated Claude Code (version 2.1.277) to support OpenAI\u0027s AGENTS.md instruction format alongside its native CLAUDE.md, so teams can maintain a single instruction file used across Claude, Codex, and other coding agents rather than keeping multiple files in sync. Behavioral differences between formats exist -- CLAUDE.md supports Claude-specific features that AGENTS.md was not designed for. Critically, AGENTS.md support requires fetching feature flags from Anthropic, so deployments via Amazon Bedrock, Google Vertex AI, or with telemetry disabled cannot access this feature.",
        "execSummary":  "Cross-agent instruction compatibility reduces a real operational burden for enterprise teams running multiple AI coding agents, and the AGENTS.md support gives a single control point for enforcing coding conventions, security guardrails, and compliance policies across the development toolchain. The deployment limitation is significant: enterprises routing Claude through Bedrock or Vertex -- common choices for data residency or security reasons -- cannot use AGENTS.md support and default back to CLAUDE.md, creating a potential inconsistency in how governance instructions are applied across agents. Enterprises considering multi-agent development platforms should verify their deployment path before relying on AGENTS.md as a unified governance mechanism. This move also signals a broader industry push toward interoperable agent instruction standards that enterprise architects should track.",
        "vendorLean":  "Anthropic",
