        "execSummary":  "This report is the most direct strategic brief Microsoft has issued for enterprise executives: companies that deploy AI agents as digital labor, not just productivity tools, are already pulling ahead. The 82% figure on rethinking strategy signals broad executive alignment, making the case internally easier but raising the stakes for laggards. For customer-support leaders specifically, the \u0027agent boss\u0027 model is immediately applicable -- supervisors shift from handling tickets to designing agent workflows and reviewing edge cases. The caveat Microsoft underplays is change management: workers need new skills to effectively direct agents, and organizations that skip workforce enablement will see poor ROI.",
