        "summary":  "Microsoft identifies seven AI trends expected to define 2026, including AI evolving from a standalone tool into a collaborative partner that amplifies human capabilities across healthcare, research, and software development. The piece highlights new security frameworks for enterprise AI agents, quantum computing advances combining AI with classical supercomputers, and medical diagnostic breakthroughs addressing global healthcare shortages. Infrastructure investment will prioritize energy efficiency and intelligent resource allocation rather than raw capacity expansion.",
        "execSummary":  "The security-framework trend for enterprise agents is the most operationally urgent item: organizations deploying agents in 2026 without governance guardrails are building technical debt that regulators and auditors will eventually unwind. The shift in infrastructure investment toward efficiency -- not just scale -- reflects a maturing market where AI unit economics are becoming a board-level metric. For customer-support leaders, the healthcare AI diagnostic parallels are instructive: the same pattern of AI handling routine analysis while humans oversee exceptions is directly applicable to support triage and resolution workflows. Microsoft\u0027s framing of AI as a collaborative partner is strategic positioning ahead of anticipated labor-displacement criticism.",
