        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s framing of AI as a platform for societal acceleration -- not just productivity -- signals how it intends to compete with Microsoft\u0027s enterprise narrative: by anchoring AI\u0027s legitimacy in demonstrable scientific outcomes. For enterprise leaders, the healthcare diagnostics examples are directly transferable as a business case template: identify high-volume, high-stakes decisions where AI can flag exceptions for human review. The 300-language expansion is a concrete capability milestone relevant to global customer-support operations where multilingual coverage is a persistent cost and quality challenge. The responsible AI caveats around accuracy and equitable access are genuine operational risks that enterprise deployments must address in SLA design, not just legal disclaimers.",
