        "summary":  "Anthropic announced Enterprise Frontier Safeguards (EFS), combining zero data retention privacy with misuse detection capabilities in a customer-controlled architecture. Customer data is stored on client-managed infrastructure rather than Anthropic\u0027s, with rollout beginning fall 2026. The solution was developed collaboratively with over 100 enterprise customers across financial services, healthcare, and manufacturing.",
        "execSummary":  "Enterprise Frontier Safeguards resolves the core tension between AI safety requirements and enterprise privacy compliance by moving security monitoring architecture directly onto customer-controlled infrastructure. Developed with CISOs from major financial institutions, EFS enables organizations to deploy advanced models while maintaining custody of activity logs and encryption keys -- a structural answer to data sovereignty requirements. Automated monitoring sends security flags directly to customer teams, eliminating Anthropic human review requirements and accelerating incident response timelines. This is a meaningful architectural shift for regulated industries and signals that enterprise AI deployment is maturing beyond policy commitments toward enforceable technical controls.",
