        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "Reactiv, a mobile commerce platform for Shopify merchants, implemented a three-agent system using Amazon Bedrock AgentCore to automate app updates, reducing merchant configuration time by 80% and accelerating production timelines by 33%. The solution unified interactive and autonomous agent capabilities on shared infrastructure with persistent memory, cutting what previously required 17 hours of manual work to just 3 hours. Annual infrastructure costs fell by approximately $6,000.",
        "execSummary":  "This case study demonstrates that multi-agent orchestration on managed infrastructure can deliver measurable ROI quickly -- 80% time savings, 33% faster production, and $6,000 in annual cost reduction for a small platform team. The elimination of 100 OpenAPI specification files and custom infrastructure overhead shows that consolidating onto a managed agent platform can meaningfully reduce engineering maintenance burden. For customer-support leaders, the persistent memory and multi-tenant data isolation capabilities are directly relevant: they enable agents to maintain context across interactions without custom state management. The 10-week deployment versus the prior 15-week timeline signals that managed agent platforms are reducing the time-to-value curve for production AI automation.",
